 a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 54     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Left   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm vertical skin ellipse  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior  deep  is inked black  lateral is green  medial is blue  and anterior is yellow  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined nodule which is 0 3cm from the closest deep and anterior margins  and away from other margins  There are few satellite nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 2cm at the superior side of the main mass but away from the margins  No Frozen Section is done  Section code  A  superior margin B E  satellite nodules F G  mass close to anterior margin H I  mass close to posterior margin J  inferior mar