ue consistent with fat necrosis and contains soft red brown tissue  The wall of the cavity averages 0 2cm  and there is surrounding dense white fibrous tissue with no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The remaining cut surfaces show unremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue  Sectioning of the lateral breast tissue reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm hemorrhagic firm area with yellow orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis  No apparent lymph nodes are grossly appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved fibrous tissue away from cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative hemorrhagic area with fat necrosis in upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of skin and anterior margin  Gross Dictation by Stephanie Kuehn  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Paula Arnell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Paula Arnell M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 56 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  RESECTION  1  TUBULAR CARCINOMA  INVASIVE   0 4CM  PRESENT LESS THAN 0 2CM FROM THE SUPERIOR MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  LOW TO INTERMEDIATE GRADE  PRESENT AT THE SUPERIOR AND LATERAL MARGINS  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by 