ne receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm lymph node  bisected entirely frozen as FX 1 now in A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a 5 x 4 x 3cm tan yellow fibrofatty piece of breast tissue with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating medial  replaced by one pin   The specimen is inked in black and sectioned to reveal a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan white firm mass abutting the posterior margin  marked by two pins   No frozen is done  The mass is 1cm away from the lateral margin  1cm away from anterior margin  1cm away from the inferior margin  0 6cm away from the superior margin  and 1 4cm from the medial margin  SECTION CODE  B  Tumor with closest with posterior margin C D  Additional sections of tumor E  Fibrous area lateral to tumor which may represent tumors most lateral extent Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  final posterior margin  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of tan yellow fibrofatty tissue  There is a stitch on the area that is most posterior from the tumor as indicated by the surgeon  The half with the stitch is inked black and the opposite half is inked in blue to reveal tan yellow lobu