y of specimen  from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end  serially sectioned  Received fresh  labeled  final margin left breast   are 2 unoriented fragments of friable fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  each of which are serially sectioned and submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  left axillary contents   are multiple portions of fibroadipose tissue aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  which are dissected and palpated to reveal multiple candidate lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 3 2cm in greatest dimension  The largest candidate node is bisected to reveal a 0 6cm in greatest dimension cavity  with peripheral yellow discoloration  consistent with fat necrosis  This area may be consistent with the site of the previous sentinel node biopsy  All candidate nods are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate intact node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing 3 candidate intact nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Each containing 1 candidate node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest candidate node  serially sectioned  Final Diagnosis by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 11 40 14AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left  Re  Excision PART B  Breast  Left  Final Margin   Excision PART C  Lymph Nodes  Left Axilla Contents   Dissection  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  11 MAY 94 at 15 35 CLINICAL DATA  A 50 year old with intraductal carcinoma with microscopic invasion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY WITH AXILLARY DISSECTION  1  BIOPSY SITE WITH FAT NECROSIS  HEMOSIDERIN DEPOSITION AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  LYMPH NODES REMOVED_DATE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  17 MAY 94 at 18 11                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast  is a 175 gram right breast  15 x 7 x 3cm  with an overlying 15 x 4cm skin ellipse and an attached 5 x 5cm axillary tail  The skin ellipse has a 1cm centrally placed  grossly unremarkable nipple with a 3 5cm straight healed biopsy scar 1 5cm medial to the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity filled with clotted blood  The biopsy site is located 0 5cm from the medial margin  3cm from the overlying skin and comes to within 0 3cm from the closest deep margin  The biopsy site is surrounded by focal tan  indurated breast tissue  The remaining breast tissue is grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal multiple tan lymph nodes  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm in diameter  Section Code A   biopsy site with closest deep margin D E   biopsy site representative sections  majority of site submitted  F   biopsy site representative section including skin G H   representative sections of unremarkable breast I   representative section of nipple J O   Axillary lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE of each Resident  Simon Bergman  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Simon Bergman  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  BARBARA LYNN SMITH  M D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results Reason for Addendum  2  Additional Fluorescence In Situ Hybridization  FISH  Results CLINICAL DATA  New calcifications  prior L cancer  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  INVASIVE AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH CALCIFICATIONS  SEE NOTE AND TABLE  1  NOTE  The invasive carcinoma has both conventional and papillary morphologies  The papillary regions demonstrate microscopically irregular contours and a complex infolding growth pattern  consistent with invasion  Immunostains for p63  calponin  SM MHC  and cytokeratin 14 fail to demonstrate myoepithelial cells around these foci  consistent with a diagnosis of invasive carcinoma when considered with the morphology  Other areas with more rounded  circumscribed nests of ductal carcinoma also lack myoepithelial cells by immunohistochemical evaluation  and these may represent ductal carcinoma in situ with marked myoepithelial cell attenuation or possibly additional bluntly invasive carcinoma  The current carcinoma demonstrates morphologic similarity to the patient s prior carcinoma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Multiple levels examined  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE  At least 0 2cm  GRADE  1  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Invasive carcinoma comes to  0 1cm from the posterior margin and to 0 12cm from the inferior margin  and a focus suspicious for invasion comes to  0 1cm from the medial margin  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  1  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Ductal carcinoma in situ comes to  0 1cm from the medial  inferior  and posterior margins  That some of these foci interpreted as in situ carcinoma may actually represent bluntly invasive carcinoma cannot be entirely excluded  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  Requested  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  left breast biopsy with needle loc   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  tan yellow to focally hemorrhagic portion of irregular fibroadipose tissue with a short suture designating superior  a long suture designating lateral  and a needle localization wire in place  The specimen is inked according to protocol  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  superior   green  inferior   yellow  and serially sectioned from medial to lateral  Sectioning reveals a lobulated  tan yellow cut surface with focal hemorrhagic areas  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The specimen is submitted entirely as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial en face margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Body of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral en face margin  The area of possible calcifications is in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1  QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  The tumor cell membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   over overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  2  RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  108  to chromosome 17 signals  105  in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be interpreted with caution  Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  report_end  , Unchecked.
