sue  The biopsy cavity measures 1 5cm in diameter and is located in the medial one half of the breast  The biopsy cavity comes to within 0 2cm of the deep inked surgical resection margin and 2 5cm from the medial resection margin  Surrounding the biopsy cavity is a firm area of tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and appears to contain calcium flecks  This firmer area is located away from the deep surgical resection margin  The remainder of the breast tissue has been sampled to reveal unremarkable fibrous breast parenchyma and unremarkable adipose tissue  Section Code  A  section through ellipse of skin showing surgical scar  B  section through nipple and areolar  C  medial resection margin  D G  biopsy cavity and adjacent firm tissue lesion  submitted in toto  showing closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin  black ink   H I  two sections through firm areas located in the upper outer quadrant  no discrete lesion  fibrous tissue  J N  lymph nodes  Labeled  Additional axillary tissue  right breast  consist of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue  REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Individual lymph nodes from this specimen are submitted entirely in cassette O  Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  ADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
