 that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 43     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue with a needle localization  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm in diameter tan white stellate firm mass abutting the inked margin  Representative sections of the mass are frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette G  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A   F  with the lesion in cassette C  and again the frozen section in cassette G  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ALEXANDER KRATZ  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FXDX  1  BREAST MASS  LEFT   PREDOMINANTLY INFILTRATING DUCTAL AND LESS EXTENSIVE INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
