s of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast excision specimen  needle localizing in place and an accompanying X ray  Specimen is oriented by the surgeon  The lateral surface inked red  the inferior surface inked yellow  the medial surface inked green  and the superior surface inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal an ill defined 1 5cm stellate area extending to within 0 1cm of the deep margin closer to the medial side  A representative section of this area is frozen as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and submitted as A  Sections adjacent to the frozen section area on the deep margin in B through E  There is a 1 0cm  somewhat hemorrhagic tan area lateral to the stellate area  along the deep margin  representative section in F  The remaining specimen is tan yellow intermixed and focally rubbery with no definite masses  Representative section from the lateral margin in G  superior in H  medial in I  and inferior in J   Axillary dissection   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm piece of adipose tissue dissected to reveal greater than 10 nodules  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in greates