formance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 14 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of breast with a short stitch indicating superior and a long stitch indicating lateral  Three needle localization wires are identified adjacent to the lateral margin  The specimen is inked as follows  medial in red  lateral in yellow  anterior in blue  posterior in black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm irregular firm area with multiple calcifications  which comes to 0 5cm from the closest posterior margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm well demarcated  tan yellow area with calcifications  which abuts the anterior  posterior  and lateral  and medial margins  Also identified is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm irregularly shaped  firm  tan yellow nodule which abuts the lateral margin and is 0 4cm from the closest posterior margin  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A K  calcified firm area is in B C  the 0 6cm nodule in D  and the 3 0cm area in E K   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  additional margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of breast with a short stitch designating the superior margin  a long stitch designating the lateral margin and a double stitch designating the edge furthest from tumor  The external surface shows a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm irregular shaped  tan white firm mass on the lateral side  The specimen is inked as follows  medial in red  lateral in yellow  anterior in blue  posterior  with double stitch  in black  Sectioning the specimen from medial to lateral reveals the tan white firm area appreciated from the external surface  which abuts all margins  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette L S  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm tan green lymph node with attached fibroadipose tissue  which is bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette T  Resident  Mari Mino  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL MARGIN   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL    report_end  , Unchecked.
