Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 20 CLINICAL DATA  Density on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  40   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  60   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor measures 0 5cm in greatest dimension by gross exam  Infiltrating carcinoma is within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The resection margin is positive for carcinoma in situ  No vascular invasion is seen  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIFHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 25     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right Breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm white firm stellate lesion that extends to the inked resection margin  Submitted entirely in A through G  with the suspicious area in C and D  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  SUSPICIOUS LESION FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  AWAIT PERMANENT SECTIONS  O R  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
