s located 0 5cm from the deep margin  and 0 2cm from the anterior margin  This biopsy cavity also has a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm hemorrhagic focus  Sectioning beneath the second scar reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm biopsy cavity  the walls of which show fat necrosis  This biopsy cavity is located approximately 4 0cm medial to the first biopsy cavity  1 1cm from the deep margin  and 0 3cm from the anterior margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast reveals yellow  fatty tissue and soft  gray white fibrous tissue  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm firm  blue gray nodule located approximately 6 0cm inferiorly from the second biopsy cavity  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary fat pad  ranging in size from 0 4cm in greatest dimension to 1 5cm in greatest dimension  One representative section of each lymph node is submitted  SECTION CODE  A B  First biopsy cavity to deep margin  C   First biopsy cavity to anterior margin  D E  First biopsy cavity  F   Skin overlying first biopsy cavity  G H  Second biopsy cavity to deep margin  I   Second biopsy cavity to anterior margin  J   Second biopsy cavity  K   Small nodule  L O  Lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional right axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of adipose tissue and lymph nodes  The lymph nodes range in size from 0 4cm to 0 7cm  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted in Cassette P  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  Edi Brogi  M D   PhD  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  ADDITIONAL     report_end  , Unchecked.
