receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 32 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm modified breast radical mastectomy specimen  which includes a REMOVED_DATE x 8 0cm axillary tail  On the specimen there is a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a 0 9cm in diameter nipple and a 2 5cm in diameter areolar complex  2 5cm from the superior skin margin  on the skin ellipse is a 0 6cm suture  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  On cross section  there is an area of firm  white tissue that is directly underneath the skin suture previously noted  This area of white  firm tissue measures a 5 0cm in width and 5 0cm in superior inferior dimension  It comes to within 1 5cm of the closest deep margin  2 5cm from the closest inferior margin  and 5 0cm from the superior margin  In this area of white  firm tissue there are areas of focal hemorrhage  There is no biopsy cavity present  SECTION CODE  A  tumor with closest deep inked margin  B D  tumor with deep inked margin  E  most lateral extension of the tumor  F  area of white  fibrous bands  medial and discontinuous with the medial extent of the tumor  G  representative section from the biopsy site  H  representative section through the nipple with underlying breast  I  skin with suture and underlying breast  J L  additional dissected lymph nodes  M  representative section from the medial margin  N  representative section from the superior margin  O  representative section from the inferior margin  P  representative section from the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse  Resident  M  Prisci