 Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 15     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT SPICULATED MASS   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  in three parts  Labeled  Left breast proximal and distal together  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of breast tissue with two localizing needles and an accompanying x ray  A black stitch designates needle  1  The superficial portion of the specimen is inked with black and the deeper portion is inked with red  Sectioning reveals two minute cysts and focal slightly firm areas  The rest of the specimen is unremarkable breast parenchyma and adipose tissue  No frozen section is done  The superficial portion inked with black is submitted in A through K  The deeper portion inked with red is submitted in L through T  The specimen is submitted entirely  Labeled   1  spiculated mass  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of fatty breast tissue with a black suture at one end  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 5cm hard nodule that is present 1 5cm from the suture and which focally approaches close to the margin  A portion is frozen as frozen section  1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of the mass and the resection margin are submitted in U  V  and W  Labeled  Right breast lateral inferior  are two pieces of breast tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Both are inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty tissue  Representative sections are submitted in X Y Z and CC  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Deep right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibrofatty tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned  It is submitted entirely in AA and BB  Gross Description by  David Weissmann  M D  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST RIGHT   1   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU CARCINOMA  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS PRESENT  GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST LATERAL INFERIOR   NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY UPPER LOWER TOGETHER PART B  RIGHT BREAST SPICULATED MASS PART C  RIGHT BREAST LATERAL INFERIOR PART D  DEEP RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
